ham Power:** It is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. It withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering because investor demand fell short. It says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. That is direct evidence of the equity route failing. It also means the planned 18% increase in 2027 capex will not go ahead as announced.\n- **Wider market:** Two other utility share offerings in Q3 2026 were cut back in size. Equity demand is weak across the sector, not just for Pellham.\n- **Norvane Utilities:** It plans 12% higher 2027 capex. I found no equity offering from it. In Q3 it priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, which suggests it can fund through debt instead.\n- **Debt market:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Debt is more expensive but still open.\n\n**Implications:**\n- Equity can still work for smaller or downsized raises, but not for large ones.\n- Expect funding to shift toward debt, with some projects deferred.\n- For anyone selling grid equipment, the Pellham cut is a downside risk to 2027 demand.\n\nSources: utility-capex-2027, pellham-offering, utility-credit.","ttft_ms":4957,"type":"result","duration_ms":23939,"uuid":"22b9bb10-569a-422c-9a89-9cb1c4ec142b","ttft_stream_ms":3480,"time_to_request_ms":237,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":48,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":9,"input_attachments":43,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":23,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":9,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":8,"request_announcements":21,"query_setup":3,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":11,"message_normalization":11,"client_creation":3,"request_build":19},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":103,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":67,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":190,"process_a